WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.850
From the outside, Asha's bottleneck looks like going live, not selling.

2
00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:10.875
Public posts mention contracted revenue piling up, and more demand than the team can onboard.

3
00:00:10.875 --> 00:00:19.600
My guess is that every new practice needs someone to turn its scripts, hours, provider lists and protocols into agent settings by hand.

4
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:21.900
This prototype tests that guess.

5
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:29.500
It compiles a practice's intake packet into an agent config, checks it, and leaves a person only the exceptions.

6
00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:34.500
Plain code handles anything that must be exact and repeatable.

7
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:38.650
The compiler parses five packet files into a typed config.

8
00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:42.100
The validator runs nine deterministic rules.

9
00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:47.075
A semantic check looks for an FAQ answer that contradicts the call script.

10
00:00:47.075 --> 00:00:50.650
That is the only place a language model is allowed.

11
00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:53.300
Each issue then gets a proposed fix.

12
00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:57.350
After that come review, a smoke test, and a gated export.

13
00:00:57.967 --> 00:01:00.817
There's no real practice data anywhere.

14
00:01:00.817 --> 00:01:04.092
A seeded generator writes six fake practices:

15
00:01:04.092 --> 00:01:10.117
internal medicine, cardiology, pulmonology, urgent care and a multispecialty group.

16
00:01:10.117 --> 00:01:15.092
Each packet ships a defects file, the answer key for the mistakes planted in it.

17
00:01:15.092 --> 00:01:20.492
Thirty in total, and one practice is deliberately clean, to catch false alarms.

18
00:01:20.492 --> 00:01:25.592
A test regenerates everything and fails if the committed data has drifted.

19
00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:31.075
Let's follow one practice, Harborview Heart Clinic, a cardiology packet.

20
00:01:31.075 --> 00:01:36.125
Load packet reads the five files as lines, and compile packet walks them.

21
00:01:36.125 --> 00:01:39.900
Line twelve of the hours file says Friday, eight to three.

22
00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:51.475
A pattern match finds the day, parse time converts the times to twenty-four hour form, and the result is a day-hours object with the source hours.txt:12.

23
00:01:51.475 --> 00:01:55.900
Pydantic requires a source on every item, and checks its format.

24
00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:59.575
Now the compiled config goes to run rules.

25
00:01:59.575 --> 00:02:01.925
Take the hours conflict rule.

26
00:02:01.925 --> 00:02:09.925
It scans every line the agent might say, script lines and FAQ answers, for phrases like "our Friday hours are".

27
00:02:09.925 --> 00:02:12.650
Line nine of the script says eight to five.

28
00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:15.150
The official hours say eight to three.

29
00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:19.925
So it raises a high-severity issue, and cites both lines as evidence.

30
00:02:19.925 --> 00:02:25.350
For this practice the checks raise seven issues, matching its seven planted defects.

31
00:02:25.967 --> 00:02:29.917
The contradiction check has two backends with the same output.

32
00:02:29.917 --> 00:02:37.792
If an LLM model is configured and LiteLLM is installed, it asks the model for contradictions as JSON.

33
00:02:37.792 --> 00:02:42.317
That reply is validated, and every cited line must exist.

34
00:02:42.317 --> 00:02:45.842
If anything fails, it falls back to a keyword mock.

35
00:02:45.842 --> 00:02:50.992
The mock runs whenever no model is set, so nothing needs a key or a network.

36
00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:58.700
Next, the repairer proposes a fix for every issue, with a confidence score and the lines it was drawn from.

37
00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:05.975
A fix is applied automatically only when confidence is at least zero point eight, and never for escalation.

38
00:03:05.975 --> 00:03:11.725
For Harborview, the Friday hours and the duplicate visit type are fixed automatically.

39
00:03:11.725 --> 00:03:20.050
The missing chest-pain rule scores exactly zero point eight, but it's escalation, so it waits for a person, along with four others.

40
00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:28.542
Reviewer decisions, accept, edit or reject, are stored in SQLite, and replayed on top of the compiled config.

41
00:03:28.542 --> 00:03:35.742
Then a smoke test sends ten scripted patient messages through a keyword router that reads only that config.

42
00:03:35.742 --> 00:03:37.767
Harborview passes nine.

43
00:03:37.767 --> 00:03:41.767
The chest-pain message finds no rule, so nothing escalates.

44
00:03:41.767 --> 00:03:46.192
And export stays blocked while any high-severity issue is open.

45
00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:50.092
Here, that's the chest-pain rule and a broken phone number.

46
00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:55.200
To try it, run make demo, and open localhost, port eight thousand.

47
00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:58.500
It needs no keys, no Node, and no network.

48
00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:00.325
There are four screens.

49
00:04:00.325 --> 00:04:03.675
Practices, with status and open exceptions.

50
00:04:03.675 --> 00:04:07.850
Packet to config, where clicking a field highlights its source line.

51
00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:12.075
Exceptions, with evidence, the proposed fix, and its confidence.

52
00:04:12.075 --> 00:04:14.900
And the smoke test, with the export button.

53
00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:18.875
Make eval scores everything against the answer key.

54
00:04:18.875 --> 00:04:24.500
In mock mode, the checks find all thirty planted defects, with no false alarms.

55
00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:31.225
All twenty-four scored fixes match the known answer, and ninety-five percent of fields need no review.

56
00:04:31.225 --> 00:04:35.075
Before review, fifty-seven of sixty smoke tests pass.

57
00:04:35.075 --> 00:04:39.425
The three failures are escalation fixes it won't apply alone.

58
00:04:39.425 --> 00:04:44.650
These numbers are optimistic, because the defects and the checks were written together.

59
00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:46.175
Other limits:

60
00:04:46.175 --> 00:04:54.675
the packet format is a guess, the red-flag lists need a physician's review, and the router matches keywords; it isn't a live agent.

61
00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:56.975
So, to recap.

62
00:04:56.975 --> 00:05:02.550
The compiler is deterministic, and every value points back to a file and a line.

63
00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:07.850
Nine rules and one semantic check turn mistakes into issues with evidence.

64
00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:12.900
Confident fixes apply themselves; escalation always waits for a person.

65
00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:16.425
And the answer key lets make eval score all of it.

66
00:05:17.033 --> 00:05:18.858
Thank you for watching.
